'''Celeste Mucci''' (born 11 August 1999) is an Australian [[sport of athletics|athlete]].<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.iaaf.org/athletes/australia/celeste-mucci-295507 |title=Celeste Mucci |publisher=IAAF |access-date=6 October 2019}}</ref> She was fourth in the [[Athletics at the 2018 Commonwealth Games – Women's heptathlon|women's heptathlon]] at the 2018 Commonwealth Games held in April in Brisbane, Australia, and was fifth in the [[2018 IAAF World U20 Championships – Women's heptathlon|women's heptathlon]] at the July 2018 IAAF World U20 Championships held in the Ratinan Stadion, Tampere, Finland. Mucci won the Australian national championships in heptathlon in 2018 and 2019.<ref>{{Cite web|url= https://worldathletics.org/athletes/australia/celeste-mucci-14555113|title=Celeste Mucci Honours|website=World Athletics}}</ref>

Mucci was part of the Australian team which won the women's {{nowrap|4 × 100 m}} relay at the [[2019 Oceania Athletics Championships]] and competed in the [[2019 World Athletics Championships – Women's 4 × 100 metres relay|women's 4 × 100 metres relay]] event at the [[2019 World Athletics Championships]].<ref>{{cite web |url=https://media.aws.iaaf.org/competitiondocuments/pdf/6033/AT-4X1-W-h----.SL2.pdf |title=4 x 100 Metres Relay Women - Round 1 |work=IAAF (Doha 2019) |access-date=6 October 2019}}</ref> She was the 2019 Australian women's 100m hurdles champion.

Mucci won the [[100m hurdles]] at the [[2022 Oceania Athletics Championships|2022 Oceania Championships]] held in June and finished seventh in the [[Athletics at the 2022 Commonwealth Games – Women's 100 metres hurdles|women's 100 metres hurdles]] at the [[2022 Commonwealth Games]] held in August in Birmingham, England.

